  "exposure": "Parent informed me prior distinct reviewer left finite mood/future unresolved. No author votes, current-English comparison, exact candidate or old semantic freeze/verdict has been opened. I independently viewed native136 then137, wrote initial tentative source freeze, then examined the actual primary photographs listed below. Lexical-head locator packet was seen between native reading and initial written freeze; labels were not a semantic verdict. This is not a claim of total blindness or human expertise.",
  "whole_baseline_source_reading": "ወይዴመሩ፡ ኵሉ፡ ማያት፡ [ዘ]ምስለ፡ ማያተ፡ ዘመልዕልተ፡ ሰማያት፡ ተባዕታይ፡ ውእቱ፡ ወማይ፡ ዘመትሕተ፡ ምድር፡ አንስታይት፡ ይእቲ።",
  "initial_reading_correction": "The initial tentative freeze wrote ደ in the first verb and left its vowel open. Direct comparison to actual TableI d-row now identifies ዴ, fifth-order dē: the lower-right square distinguishes it from first-order ደ. The initial artifact remains unchanged as history.",
  "finite_form": {
    "printed_form": "ወይዴመሩ",
    "segmentation": "ወ + ይዴመሩ; wa + yəddēmäru (phonological doubled d from assimilation; not a printed gemination mark).",
    "lexical_control": "Dillmann Lexicon actual columns1086->1087: ደመረ I,2; reflexive-passive ተደመረ explicitly III,2. Full continuation at1087 has misceri, commisceri, admisceri, immisceri for liquids and wider joining/mixing associations; no need to derive form or mood from the Hen54:8 citation.",
    "stem": "III,2, reflexive/passive of intensive stem, not III,1.",
    "assimilation": "Actual photograph filed as printed101-leaf0137.png is physically printed103, §54. It states reflexive t assimilates to radical d; §97 printed191 repeats t-assimilation before dental-lingual. Thus yət-dēmäru -> yəddēmäru explains absence of written t without deleting it arbitrarily.",
    "mood": "Imperfect/indicative, not subjunctive: §97 actual printed195 contrasts III,2 imperfect ē after first radical (second radical loses doubling) with subjunctive a after first radical (second radical doubled). Source fifth-order ዴ is positive evidence for ē. The III,1 syncretism described at191–194 is not applicable to this III,2 form.",
    "person_number": "Third-person masculine plural: yə prefix plus final ū; actual §101 printed203–204 establishes prefix and plural ending. Source is ru (second vowel order), not rā or r zero.",
    "future_force": "§89 printed169 states imperfect is the ordinary future expression, absolute or relative;170 continues uses and contrasts volition. The unit opens with simple coordinating wa, not a purpose/wish/subjunctive governor. Native54:7 supplies the temporal frame in those days, continued into8 and9. Therefore predictive will be mingled / will mingle is warranted here, not a command let them mingle and not perfect were mingled.",
    "limit": "Mood is resolved by the actual written vowel and paradigm; future time remains a contextual semantic reading as in any translation, not a separate special future suffix."
  },
